# Tiny test circuit: each pair of data qubits is prepared in a +1
# eigenstate of the corresponding 2-body Pauli (XX, ZZ, YY) using only
# single-qubit ops, then that Pauli is measured twice via MPP. The two
# measurements should agree, so each DETECTOR (rec[-1] XOR rec[-2]) is
# deterministic. After Bell translation the DETECTOR refs are rewritten
# to two pairs of ancilla recs, but the detector value is preserved.

# XX block on qubits 0, 1: |++> is a +1 eigenstate of XX.
RX 0 1
MXX 0 1
DETECTOR rec[-1]
MPP X0*X1
DETECTOR rec[-1] rec[-2]

# ZZ block on qubits 2, 3: |00> is a +1 eigenstate of ZZ.
R 2 3
MZZ 2 3
DETECTOR rec[-1]
MPP Z2*Z3
DETECTOR rec[-1] rec[-2]

# YY block on qubits 4, 5: H S |0> = |+i> is a +1 eigenstate of Y, so
# |+i, +i> is a +1 eigenstate of YY.
R 4 5
H 4 5
S 4 5
MPP Y4*Y5
DETECTOR rec[-1]
MPP Y4*Y5
DETECTOR rec[-1] rec[-2]
